00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:06.120
Even if you need a pen that's right next to it.
即使你需要的那支笔就在它旁边。

173
00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:10.220
Even if I need a pen, I will just block it with my hand as I reach across for the pen.
即使我需要那支笔，我在伸手去拿笔的时候也会用手挡住它。

174
00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:14.800
But if it's a Michael Scott-esque person, you might need to.
但如果是迈克尔·斯科特那种人，你可能就得看了。

175
00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:16.040
I might need to look at it.
我可能确实得看看。

176
00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:16.400
Okay.
好吧。

177
00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:17.780
That's fine.
没问题。

178
00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:18.300
Okay.
好吧。

179
00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:20.300
Anyway, that's a very interesting question.
总之，这是一个非常有趣的问题。

180
00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:21.900
I'm not a snoop lady.
我可不是个爱打探的人。

181
00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:24.540
If it's out there in my face, I'm going to look at it.
如果它就摆在那儿，正对着我，我肯定会看的。

182
00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:26.080
And who can blame you?
谁又能怪你呢？

183
00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:26.720
Thank you.
谢谢。

184
00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:30.160
Lastly, you guys, I found a great talking head by Toby
最后，伙计们，我找到了托比的一段精彩采访片段

185
00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:31.560
and the candy bag alts.
还有糖果袋的备选镜头。

186
00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:35.360
It would have come right after they read from Michael's journal
它本该出现在他们读完迈克尔日记之后

187
00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:36.320
in the deposition.
在证词陈述环节里。

188
00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:37.980
And here's what it said.
内容是这样的。

189
00:06:38.140 --> 00:06:39.340
I think it's so damn funny.
我觉得太搞笑了。

190
00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:41.520
Toby looks directly to
托比直接看向了

191
00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:42.300
the camera crew.
摄影组。

192
00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:44.360
God bless you.
上帝保佑你们。

193
00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:48.520
God bless you for recording this today for all time.
上帝保佑你们今天把这一切永远记录了下来。

194
00:06:50.060 --> 00:06:53.040
That does make me laugh.
那确实让我笑了。

195
00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:57.140
All right, everybody.
好了，各位。

196
00:06:57.160 --> 00:07:00.240
Here is our breakdown of the deposition.
这是我们对证词陈述环节的分析。

197
00:07:28.950 --> 00:07:29.830
Very important.
非常重要。

198
00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:33.950
We have to do a very important legal procedure.
我们必须进行一项非常重要的法律程序。

199
00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:35.310
Oh, Lord.
天哪。

200
00:07:35.410 --> 00:07:36.750
I was like, wait, what's happening?
我当时心想，等等，发生什么事了？

201
00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:38.930
And then I realized you're talking about the episode.
然后我才意识到你在说那一集。

202
00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:40.010
The deposition.
《证词》那一集。

203
00:07:40.470 --> 00:07:41.870
I was like, Jenna, what do we have to do?
我当时心想，珍娜，我们得做什么？

204
00:07:42.050 --> 00:07:42.890
Did I miss an email?
我是不是漏看了什么邮件？

205
00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:43.850
What's happening?
发生什么事了？

206
00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:44.570
No.
没有。

207
00:07:44.850 --> 00:07:47.450
We have a very important deposition today, Angela.
安吉拉，我们今天有个非常重要的证词录制。

208
00:07:47.670 --> 00:07:49.450
It's season four, episode 12.
是第四季第12集。

209
00:07:50.010 --> 00:07:50.970
Written by?
编剧是谁？

210
00:07:51.210 --> 00:07:52.110
Lester Lewis.
莱斯特·刘易斯。

211
00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:54.510
Directed by Julian Farino.
导演是朱利安·法里诺。

212
00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:55.950
Hit me with a summary.
给我讲讲剧情梗概。

213
00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:57.050
Here it is.
内容是这样的。

214
00:07:57.230 --> 00:08:02.690
Michael and Jan go to corporate, and Michael is deposed as a witness in Jan's
迈克尔和简去了总公司，迈克尔作为证人出席了简的

215
00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:05.690
wrongful termination case against Dunder Mifflin.
针对邓德·米夫林公司的非法解雇诉讼。

216
00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:07.070
What was Jan thinking?
简到底在想什么？

217
00:08:07.370 --> 00:08:10.510
Why would you ever put Michael on any kind of witness stand?
她怎么会想让迈克尔去当证人呢？

218
00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:11.870
I don't know.
我不知道。

219
00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:13.570
I'm so glad she did.
但我很高兴她这么做了。

220
00:08:15.410 --> 00:08:19.310
Well, while they're gone, Jim and Daryl play ping pong in the warehouse,
嗯，在他们离开期间，吉姆和达里尔在仓库打乒乓球，

221
00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:23.490
which sparks a rivalry between Pam and Kelly.
这引发了帕姆和凯莉之间的竞争。

222
00:08:25.710 --> 00:08:31.610
Fast fact number one this week, Angela, is Lester Lewis, the writer of this episode.
本周第一个冷知识，安吉拉，是关于这一集的编剧莱斯特·刘易斯。

223
00:08:32.050 --> 00:08:37.930
Before writing on The Office, Lester had worked on The Larry Sanders Show and Caroline in the City.
在为《办公室》写剧本之前，莱斯特曾参与过《拉里·桑德斯秀》和《卡罗琳在城里》的制作。

224
00:08:38.170 --> 00:08:43.950
He was one of the original members of our writing team going back to season one.
他是我们从第一季开始的原始编剧团队成员之一。

225
00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:47.170
And this is a tough one for me, Ange.
说到这个我很难过，安吉。

226
00:08:48.030 --> 00:08:55.070
For both of us, I know Lester passed away in 2013, and I don't even know where to start.
我们俩都很难过，我知道莱斯特在2013年去世了，我甚至不知道该从何说起。

227
00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:57.290
I loved him.
我爱他。

228
00:08:57.510 --> 00:08:58.530
I loved this man.
我深爱着这个人。

229
00:08:58.770 --> 00:09:03.110
We bonded over our love of autobiographical comic books.
我们因为对自传体漫画书的共同爱好而结缘。

230
00:09:03.110 --> 00:09:09.130
We both loved those, and I just have such fond memories of being with him.
我们都喜欢那些书，我对和他在一起的时光有着非常美好的回忆。

231
00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:14.210
And he was so funny, and he was so just kind and warm.
他非常风趣，而且为人特别善良、温暖。

232
00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:15.730
He was so kind.
他真的非常善良。

233
00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:18.030
And just a good, good person.
他就是一个非常好、非常好的人。

234
00:09:18.750 --> 00:09:19.650
And I miss him.
我很想念他。

235
00:09:20.150 --> 00:09:20.430
Yeah.
是啊。

236
00:09:20.710 --> 00:09:23.370
I mean, Lester was someone that made time for everyone.
我是说，莱斯特是一个会为每个人留出时间的人。

237
00:09:23.550 --> 00:09:24.350
You know those people?
你知道那种人吗？

238
00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:25.810
They make time for everybody.
他们会为每个人留出时间。

239
00:09:25.810 --> 00:09:28.950
And he was just a wonderful part of our show.
他曾是我们剧组非常棒的一员。

240
00:09:29.450 --> 00:09:33.410
I re-listened to the DVD commentary for this particular episode.
我重听了这一集的DVD评论音轨。

241
00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:35.110
Lester is in the commentary.
莱斯特就在评论音轨里。

242
00:09:35.570 --> 00:09:40.570
And it was so wonderful to hear his voice and also made me sad.
听到他的声音感觉很棒，但也让我感到难过。

243
00:09:40.570 --> 00:09:41.410
It was bittersweet.
那是一种苦乐参半的感觉。

244
00:09:41.590 --> 00:09:46.690
But if you listen to the DVD commentary for this episode, you will just hear what a thoughtful person he was.
但如果你听这一集的DVD评论音轨，你就能听出他是一个多么体贴的人。

245
00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:51.670
And I'll share a few of the things that he said on the commentary as we record today, Jenna.
今天录制的时候，我会分享一些他在评论音轨里说过的话，珍娜。

246
00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:52.870
I love that.
我喜欢这样。

247
00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:55.690
Well, lady, what is your fast fact number two?
那么，女士，你的第二个冷知识是什么？

248
00:09:55.810 --> 00:09:59.010
You know, ping pong features very heavily in this episode.
你知道，这一集里乒乓球占了很大篇幅。

249
00:09:59.270 --> 00:10:03.090
So I felt we needed a little history of ping pong.
所以我感觉我们需要了解一点乒乓球的历史。

250
00:10:03.310 --> 00:10:03.930
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

251
00:10:04.010 --> 00:10:05.770
Did someone do a deep dive on ping pong?
有人深入研究过乒乓球吗？

252
00:10:06.010 --> 00:10:06.450
I did.
我研究过。

253
00:10:06.470 --> 00:10:09.430
I want you to know it has two other names.
我想让你知道它还有另外两个名字。

254
00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:10.230
Oh.
哦。

255
00:10:10.650 --> 00:10:12.890
Table tennis or whiff-waff.
桌球或“威夫-瓦夫”（whiff-waff）。

256
00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:14.090
Whiff-waff?
威夫-瓦夫？

257
00:10:14.230 --> 00:10:15.310
That sounds made up.
听起来像是编出来的。

258
00:10:15.490 --> 00:10:17.370
Do you want to play some whiff-waff?
你想打会儿“威夫-瓦夫”吗？

259
00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:19.550
I'll play you some wooffle whiff-waff.
我要跟你打几局“呜呼威夫-瓦夫”。

260
00:10:20.770 --> 00:10:21.610
Oh, dear.
天哪。

261
00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:23.090
I'll chunk it at you.
我要把它朝你扔过去。

262
00:10:23.750 --> 00:10:25.370
What else you got about ping pong?
关于乒乓球你还知道些什么？

263
00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:28.150
Ping pong began in Victorian England.
乒乓球起源于维多利亚时代的英国。

264
00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:32.050
I know you'll like the sound of that, Angela, in the 1880s.
我知道你会喜欢这个背景的，安吉拉，那是在19世纪80年代。

265
00:10:32.710 --> 00:10:37.650
When lawn tennis players adapted their game to play indoors during the winter.
当时草地网球运动员为了在冬天也能打球，将这项运动改到了室内。

266
00:10:38.230 --> 00:10:38.590
Oh.
哦。

267
00:10:38.590 --> 00:10:40.610
Where's my Netflix show about that?
讲这个的网飞剧集在哪儿呢？

268
00:10:40.930 --> 00:10:41.150
Right?
对吧？

269
00:10:41.690 --> 00:10:42.370
Whiff-waff.
威夫-瓦夫。

270
00:10:42.610 --> 00:10:43.510
Episode one.
第一集。

271
00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:48.550
The Duke of Edinburgh comes to play whiff-waff.
爱丁堡公爵来打威夫-瓦夫。

272
00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:56.070
The game quickly caught on, and as early as 1901, tournaments were being conducted with
这项运动很快流行起来，早在1901年，锦标赛就已经有

273
00:10:56.070 --> 00:10:58.010
over 300 participants.
超过300名参赛者了。

274
00:10:58.610 --> 00:11:05.790
In 1902, a visiting Japanese university professor took the game back to Japan, where he introduced
1902年，一位来访的日本大学教授将这项运动带回了日本，并在那里向

275
00:11:05.790 --> 00:11:07.990
it to Japanese university students.
日本大学生们介绍了它。

276
00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:12.290
The first world championships were held in London in 1927.
第一届世界锦标赛于1927年在伦敦举行。

277
00:11:12.290 --> 00:11:16.050
They were won by a Hungarian, Dr. Jacoby.
冠军是一位匈牙利人，雅各比博士。

278
00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:17.130
Congratulations.
恭喜。

279
00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:18.550
Dr. Jacoby.
雅各比博士。

280
00:11:18.810 --> 00:11:19.130
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

281
00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:23.150
You go to see him for a checkup, but little do you know, he's a ping pong master.
你去找他做检查，却不知道他其实是一位乒乓球大师。

282
00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:24.490
That's right.
没错。

283
00:11:24.790 --> 00:11:31.750
The Olympic Games started featuring ping pong for the first time in 1988 in Seoul.
奥林匹克运动会于1988年在首尔首次将乒乓球列为比赛项目。

284
00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:38.090
The television coverage of the men's singles final attracted a worldwide audience of two
男子单打决赛的电视转播吸引了全球两

285
00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:39.110
billion.
十亿观众。

286
00:11:39.570 --> 00:11:40.130
Wow.
哇。

287
00:11:40.710 --> 00:11:41.110
Yeah.
是啊。

288
00:11:41.490 --> 00:11:43.550
Here was something I found very interesting.
我发现了一件非常有趣的事。

289
00:11:43.790 --> 00:11:48.610
There are many different ways to grip the paddle, and all of those grips have names.
握拍的方式有很多种，而且每种握法都有名字。

290
00:11:49.130 --> 00:11:49.790
Oh, gosh.
天哪。

291
00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:51.210
Here's how you can hold it.
你可以这样拿球拍。

292
00:11:51.610 --> 00:11:56.810
You can give it the old pen hold, the shake hand, or the sea miller.
你可以用传统的直拍、横拍，或者“西米勒”握法。

293
00:11:56.810 --> 00:12:02.870
The sea miller is actually named after an American table tennis champ, Danny Sea Miller, because
“西米勒”握法其实是以美国乒乓球冠军丹尼·西米勒的名字命名的，因为

294
00:12:02.870 --> 00:12:04.210
that's how he held his paddle.
他就是那样握拍的。

295
00:12:04.450 --> 00:12:06.090
He puts his little finger out.
他把小指伸出来。

296
00:12:06.270 --> 00:12:07.390
That's what she said.
她也是这么说的。

297
00:12:09.870 --> 00:12:12.890
There are also a bunch of different strokes.
还有很多种不同的击球方式。

298
00:12:13.370 --> 00:12:13.850
Oh, gosh.
天哪。

299
00:12:14.090 --> 00:12:15.150
That's what she said.
她也是这么说的。

300
00:12:15.570 --> 00:12:16.010
Oh, Lord.
天呐。

301
00:12:16.370 --> 00:12:21.410
There are offensive strokes, the hit, the loop, the counter hit, the flip, the smash.
进攻型击球包括：扣杀、弧圈球、反击、挑打和重扣。

302
00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:26.930
Then there's defensive strokes called the push, the chop, the block, and the lob.
还有防守型击球，比如搓球、削球、挡球和高吊球。

303
00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:32.610
And the biggest part of the game, the biggest thing that these guys work on is their spin.
这项运动最核心的部分，也是这些人最下功夫钻研的，就是旋转。

304
00:12:32.950 --> 00:12:38.710
And you can do a top spin, a back spin, a side spin, and a cork spin.
你可以打出上旋球、下旋球、侧旋球和螺旋球。

305
00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:41.630
Do you remember how good Forrest Gump was at ping pong?
你还记得《阿甘正传》里的阿甘乒乓球打得有多好吗？

306
00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:42.470
Yeah.
记得。

307
00:12:42.830 --> 00:12:44.070
He was so good.
他打得太棒了。

308
00:12:44.310 --> 00:12:46.150
I wonder if he was using the sea miller.
我在想他当时用的是不是“海米勒”打法。

309
00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:47.650
Maybe the pen hold.
也许是直拍握法。

310
00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:48.510
I don't know.
我也不确定。

311
00:12:48.650 --> 00:12:53.210
I think you do know that my husband turned our beautiful dining table into a ping pong table.
我觉得你肯定知道我丈夫把我们那张漂亮的餐桌改成了乒乓球桌。

312
00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:54.830
Lady, I know this.
女士，我知道这事。

313
00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:58.950
I watched this happen, and I knew you were going to regret it.
我亲眼看着它发生，当时我就知道你会后悔的。

314
00:12:59.110 --> 00:13:03.310
You guys were real excited, and I thought, hmm, that's going to come back.
你们当时特别兴奋，我心想，嗯，这事儿以后肯定有得受。

315
00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:05.070
They haven't regretted it, Jenna.
他们可没后悔，珍娜。

316
00:13:05.390 --> 00:13:07.370
There's only one person that regrets it.
后悔的只有一个人。

317
00:13:07.530 --> 00:13:09.650
Can we explain what Angela did, guys?
伙计们，我们要不要解释一下安吉拉做了什么？

318
00:13:09.650 --> 00:13:11.210
Here's what her family did.
这就是她家人干的好事。

319
00:13:11.210 --> 00:13:17.070
They got one of these ping pong table tops that fits over her kitchen table.
他们买了一个能架在餐桌上的乒乓球台面。

320
00:13:17.590 --> 00:13:20.070
It's meant to go over a pool table, right?
那本来是设计给台球桌用的，对吧？

321
00:13:20.350 --> 00:13:20.670
Oh.
噢。

322
00:13:20.850 --> 00:13:25.010
It's meant to set on top of a pool table, and you just put it on top of your dining table.
它是设计用来放在台球桌上的，结果他们直接把它架在了餐桌上。

323
00:13:25.230 --> 00:13:28.090
Of course, it doesn't fit our dining table, so it hangs off.
当然，它和我们的餐桌尺寸不符，所以边缘都悬空了。

324
00:13:28.310 --> 00:13:31.450
Well, also, now, guys, she has nowhere to eat.
而且，伙计们，现在她连吃饭的地方都没有了。

325
00:13:31.810 --> 00:13:32.250
Okay?
好吗？

326
00:13:32.570 --> 00:13:35.130
Angela, this is now your dining table.
安吉拉，这就是你现在的餐桌了。

327
00:13:35.130 --> 00:13:38.350
Well, it's just, it's so, I don't know.
哎呀，就是，怎么说呢，我也不知道。

328
00:13:38.650 --> 00:13:40.330
Josh and the kids love it.
乔什和孩子们都很喜欢。

329
