00:33:46.430 --> 00:33:52.950
Ladies and gentlemen of the table, I would just like to say what a joy it is for me to
桌前的各位女士、各位先生，我只想说，今天能在这里，

814
00:33:52.950 --> 00:33:53.630
be here today.
我感到非常高兴。

815
00:33:53.990 --> 00:33:56.530
But frankly, at my age, it's a joy to be anywhere.
但坦白说，以我的年纪，能去哪儿我都觉得高兴。

816
00:33:58.520 --> 00:34:02.280
I'm only 44, so I'm not old, and I guess that doesn't really play.
我才44岁，所以我并不老，我想这个笑话没起到效果。

817
00:34:03.420 --> 00:34:09.200
But the point is, I have a sense of humor, and I implore you all to have a sense of humor
但重点是，我有幽默感，我也恳求你们大家同样具备幽默感。

818
00:34:09.200 --> 00:34:09.700
as well.
也一样。

819
00:34:11.780 --> 00:34:17.600
Jan, David, my wonderful girlfriend, my gorgeous company.
简，大卫，我出色的女朋友，我华丽的公司。

820
00:34:18.700 --> 00:34:25.680
Why don't we all just take a big, deep breath, and just relax?
我们为什么不一起深吸一口气，放松一下呢？

821
00:34:31.910 --> 00:34:32.090
Good.
很好。

822
00:34:32.510 --> 00:34:33.870
That feels good.
感觉不错。

823
00:34:36.640 --> 00:34:37.840
Everybody feel better?
大家都感觉好点了吗？

824
00:34:38.200 --> 00:34:42.980
I don't know where to begin.
我不知道该从何说起。

825
00:34:43.520 --> 00:34:45.560
He tries to do a joke.
他试图讲个笑话。

826
00:34:45.560 --> 00:34:46.840
It doesn't land.
但没人买账。

827
00:34:46.840 --> 00:34:51.100
Everyone is looking at him like they're dead inside.
每个人看着他，眼神都像死了一样。

828
00:34:51.260 --> 00:34:51.760
You know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

829
00:34:51.760 --> 00:34:53.100
They have that kind of gaze.
他们就是那种眼神。

830
00:34:53.100 --> 00:34:56.740
And then he's like, okay, that didn't play.
然后他就像是，好吧，那个笑话没奏效。

831
00:34:57.100 --> 00:34:59.380
Then he implores them to have a sense of humor.
接着他恳求他们要有幽默感。

832
00:34:59.520 --> 00:35:00.780
It's a deposition.
这可是证词陈述环节。

833
00:35:01.420 --> 00:35:03.460
Should we talk about his testimony?
我们要谈谈他的证词吗？

834
00:35:03.940 --> 00:35:09.440
One thing I would like to point out, as Jan does her talking head at 6 minutes, 35 seconds,
有一点我想指出，当简在6分35秒进行个人访谈时，

835
00:35:09.820 --> 00:35:12.200
you know Corporate has a name for their conference room, Jenna?
你知道公司总部有给他们的会议室命名吗，珍娜？

836
00:35:12.440 --> 00:35:13.060
Did you know that?
你知道吗？

837
00:35:13.460 --> 00:35:13.680
What?
什么？

838
00:35:14.060 --> 00:35:16.440
Yeah, Corporate's conference room has a plaque.
是的，公司总部的会议室有一块牌匾。

839
00:35:16.640 --> 00:35:17.320
It has a name.
它有个名字。

840
00:35:17.560 --> 00:35:18.260
Do you want to hear it?
你想听听吗？

841
00:35:18.580 --> 00:35:18.980
What?
什么？

842
00:35:19.240 --> 00:35:22.620
It is the Robert Mifflin Memorial Conference Room.
那是“罗伯特·米夫林纪念会议室”。

843
00:35:23.100 --> 00:35:25.920
Is that hanging on a plaque over Jan's shoulder?
那块牌匾是挂在简肩膀上方的墙上吗？

844
00:35:26.300 --> 00:35:26.760
Yes.
是的。

845
00:35:27.540 --> 00:35:28.740
Great catch.
观察得真仔细。

846
00:35:29.180 --> 00:35:29.800
Thank you.
谢谢。

847
00:35:30.020 --> 00:35:32.620
I love me the plaques on the walls, guys.
伙计们，我超爱墙上的那些牌匾。

848
00:35:33.080 --> 00:35:39.560
As Michael's testimony begins, he very quickly gives a that's what she said joke.
迈克尔的证词刚开始，他很快就讲了一个“她就是这么说的”笑话。

849
00:35:40.100 --> 00:35:40.880
I know.
我知道。

850
00:35:41.140 --> 00:35:47.100
And it completely derails the deposition because the lawyers take everything literally.
这彻底破坏了证词陈述的进程，因为律师们把一切都当真了。

851
00:35:47.600 --> 00:35:48.700
They're like, who said that?
他们就像在说，是谁说的？

852
00:35:48.860 --> 00:35:49.620
Who is she?
她是谁？

853
00:35:49.800 --> 00:35:50.600
Who is she?
她是谁？

854
00:35:50.740 --> 00:35:51.780
And what did she say?
她说了什么？

855
00:35:51.780 --> 00:35:54.060
Here's the question the lawyer asked.
这是律师问的问题。

856
00:35:54.320 --> 00:35:57.840
And you were directly under her the entire time, Michael.
迈克尔，你全程都在她手下工作。

857
00:35:58.080 --> 00:35:59.040
That's what she said.
她就是这么说的。

858
00:36:04.030 --> 00:36:04.530
Amazing.
太绝了。

859
00:36:04.970 --> 00:36:08.510
All of their line of questioning to Michael was so good.
他们对迈克尔的所有盘问都太精彩了。

860
00:36:08.850 --> 00:36:13.670
At 7 minutes, 8 seconds, the lawyer says, how long have you known the plaintiff?
在7分08秒，律师问，你认识原告多久了？

861
00:36:13.750 --> 00:36:18.090
And Michael says, I haven't actually seen it, but I have seen the firm and I am planning
迈克尔说，我其实没看过那本书，但我看过那家律所，我正打算

862
00:36:18.090 --> 00:36:19.550
on renting the Pelican brief.
去租《塘鹅暗杀令》来看。

863
00:36:20.990 --> 00:36:22.370
Oh, my God.
天哪。

864
00:36:23.050 --> 00:36:27.710
By the way, I don't think John Grisham has a book called The Plaintiff.
顺便说一下，我觉得约翰·格里森没有一本书叫《原告》。

865
00:36:27.910 --> 00:36:28.630
He should.
他应该写一本。

866
00:36:28.910 --> 00:36:30.150
It's called The Client.
那本书叫《委托人》。

867
00:36:31.010 --> 00:36:31.890
That's right.
没错。

868
00:36:32.290 --> 00:36:33.010
It's not.
不是那本。

869
00:36:33.210 --> 00:36:34.610
I read them all.
我全读过。

870
00:36:34.830 --> 00:36:35.630
I want you to know.
我想让你知道这一点。

871
00:36:35.630 --> 00:36:42.710
So, I really appreciated in this whole episode, I really appreciated the callbacks.
所以，我真的很欣赏这一整集里的那些前后呼应。

872
00:36:43.510 --> 00:36:45.950
Yes, they were so well thought out.
是的，它们构思得太巧妙了。

873
00:36:46.210 --> 00:36:53.890
A big one comes up in this scene when Michael displays his document that he signed for HR,
这一幕里有一个重大的呼应，就是迈克尔展示了他签给HR的那份文件，

874
00:36:54.110 --> 00:36:55.070
his love document.
那份“爱情文件”。

875
00:36:55.870 --> 00:36:59.270
It's a callback from cocktails because it's in a frame.
这是对《鸡尾酒会》那一集的呼应，因为它被装在相框里。

876
00:36:59.570 --> 00:37:02.190
Michael said he was going to frame it, and he did.
迈克尔说过他要把它装裱起来，他确实做了。

877
00:37:02.490 --> 00:37:03.590
There it is, framed.
你看，装裱好了。

878
00:37:04.450 --> 00:37:08.090
And he didn't bother to take it out of the frame to bring it to the deposition.
而且他甚至懒得把它从相框里拿出来带去作证现场。

879
00:37:08.090 --> 00:37:09.790
He brought it in the frame.
他就连着相框一起带去了。

880
00:37:10.150 --> 00:37:18.690
Also, Angela, at 8 minutes, 48 seconds, there is a super cool Dunder Mifflin mug on the table
还有，安吉拉，在8分48秒，迈克尔面前的桌子上有一个超级酷的邓德·米夫林马克杯，

881
00:37:18.690 --> 00:37:19.490
in front of Michael.
就在他面前。

882
00:37:19.730 --> 00:37:20.550
Did you see it?
你看到了吗？

883
00:37:20.890 --> 00:37:23.730
It's black with silver letters.
它是黑色的，上面有银色的字母。

884
00:37:23.730 --> 00:37:28.090
I did see it, and I thought, well, Fancy Corporate has fancy mugs.
我看到了，我当时想，好吧，高级公司就是有高级马克杯。

885
00:37:28.570 --> 00:37:30.030
I want this mug.
我想要这个杯子。

886
00:37:30.070 --> 00:37:33.450
I don't think they ever did merch of this mug.
我觉得他们从来没出过这款杯子的周边。

887
00:37:33.650 --> 00:37:34.970
What a missed opportunity.
真是错失良机。

888
00:37:35.070 --> 00:37:36.510
It's a classy mug.
这杯子很有格调。

889
00:37:36.650 --> 00:37:37.370
I loved it.
我太喜欢了。

890
00:37:37.810 --> 00:37:39.270
Yeah, we never got one.
是啊，我们从来没拿到过一个。

891
00:37:39.570 --> 00:37:42.570
No, we always got the white mug with the blue letters.
没有，我们拿到的总是那种白底蓝字的杯子。

892
00:37:42.770 --> 00:37:46.390
I want the corporate mug with the silver letters, please.
请给我那个银色字母的公司马克杯吧。

893
00:37:47.670 --> 00:37:50.830
Michael has one line, Jenna, that I had to write down.
珍娜，迈克尔有一句台词，我不得不记下来。

894
00:37:51.050 --> 00:37:52.590
8 minutes, 28 seconds.
8分28秒。

895
00:37:52.590 --> 00:37:56.290
To be delicate, they hang off my lady's cheSt.
委婉点说，它们挂在我女士的胸前。

896
00:37:56.810 --> 00:38:08.430
Oh, his whole description of Jan's breasts, you know, when he's trying to explain that he thinks she got fired because she got breast implants.
噢，他描述简胸部的那整段话，你知道的，当他试图解释他认为她被解雇是因为做了隆胸手术时。

897
00:38:08.430 --> 00:38:11.470
But he won't just say that sentence.
但他就是不肯直说那句话。

898
00:38:11.710 --> 00:38:15.090
He says it's because of the twins.
他说是因为“双胞胎”。

899
00:38:15.510 --> 00:38:17.610
They hang off my lady's cheSt.
它们挂在我女士的胸前。

900
00:38:17.850 --> 00:38:18.550
To be delicate.
委婉点说。

901
00:38:18.970 --> 00:38:20.130
They make milk.
它们产奶。

902
00:38:22.270 --> 00:38:25.190
And they're like, what is this guy talking about?
他们当时心想，这家伙在说什么呢？

903
00:38:25.190 --> 00:38:31.430
All right, this deposition is going to continue, but I do think we need to check in on the folks back in Scranton.
好了，这次取证还要继续，但我确实觉得我们需要看看斯克兰顿那边的情况。

904
00:38:32.050 --> 00:38:38.910
Pam has gone around and has been recruiting people to practice ping pong in the conference room with Jim.
帕姆到处招募人手，去会议室和吉姆练习乒乓球。

905
00:38:39.410 --> 00:38:45.930
She gets Kevin to go in there by saying Jim needs help processing his travel receipts.
她骗凯文进去，说吉姆需要人帮忙处理差旅报销单。

906
00:38:45.930 --> 00:38:51.110
Well, this completely confuses Angela and Oscar because you would never ask Kevin to do this.
嗯，这让安吉拉和奥斯卡完全困惑了，因为你绝不会找凯文做这种事。

907
00:38:51.290 --> 00:38:55.930
At 6 minutes, 58 seconds, there is a shot of Angela and Oscar looking very suspicious.
在6分58秒时，有一个安吉拉和奥斯卡看起来非常怀疑的镜头。

908
00:38:56.230 --> 00:38:58.430
Why is Kevin being called to do anything?
为什么会叫凯文去做任何事？

909
00:38:58.830 --> 00:39:02.010
The shot is cropped so high, Jenna, that you don't see my belly.
那个镜头剪裁得太高了，珍娜，你看不到我的肚子。

910
00:39:02.430 --> 00:39:06.450
And also, baby jazz poster is there.
而且，那个婴儿爵士乐海报也在那儿。

911
00:39:06.910 --> 00:39:07.850
Still there.
还在那儿。

912
00:39:08.130 --> 00:39:08.750
Still there.
还在那儿。

913
00:39:09.590 --> 00:39:13.730
You and Oscar have worked something out in regard to the baby jazz poster.
你和奥斯卡关于那张婴儿爵士乐海报达成了某种共识。

914
00:39:13.730 --> 00:39:14.550
We'll never know.
我们永远不会知道。

915
00:39:14.770 --> 00:39:15.770
We never know.
我们永远不知道。

916
00:39:15.910 --> 00:39:17.330
But it's made it back on the wall.
但它又回到了墙上。

917
00:39:17.670 --> 00:39:23.510
I love the scene with Kelly and Pam in the doorway to the bathroom.
我喜欢凯莉和帕姆在洗手间门口的那场戏。

918
00:39:24.110 --> 00:39:25.650
Pam's leaving the bathroom.
帕姆正要走出洗手间。

919
00:39:25.950 --> 00:39:27.410
Kelly's entering the bathroom.
凯莉正要走进洗手间。

920
00:39:27.410 --> 00:39:29.090
And they meet in the doorway.
她们在门口相遇了。

921
00:39:29.610 --> 00:39:32.090
Who is going to let the other go by?
谁会让对方先过呢？

922
00:39:32.370 --> 00:39:37.930
Now, of course, custom would have it that you let a person exit, right?
当然，按照惯例，你应该让出来的人先走，对吧？

923
00:39:37.930 --> 00:39:39.430
Same with elevators.
电梯也是一样。

924
00:39:39.630 --> 00:39:41.790
Let the people get off before you push on.
让人先出来，你再进去。

925
00:39:42.490 --> 00:39:44.310
Yes, that's social etiquette.
是的，那是社交礼仪。

926
00:39:44.770 --> 00:39:46.570
Yeah, but there's a standoff.
没错，但她们僵持住了。

927
00:39:46.990 --> 00:39:52.730
So Pam moves aside and Kelly's like, yeah, that's what I thought.
于是帕姆让到一边，凯莉心想，哼，我就知道会这样。

928
00:39:53.410 --> 00:39:57.950
Kelly is so, like, aggressive in this whole episode.
凯莉在这一整集里都表现得太强势了。

929
00:39:58.450 --> 00:40:00.430
She's just, like, hardcore.
她简直太强硬了。

930
00:40:01.090 --> 00:40:02.810
She's working some stuff out.
她正试图解决一些问题。

931
00:40:03.290 --> 00:40:03.930
Clearly.
显而易见。

932
00:40:04.350 --> 00:40:09.330
Before we go back to the deposition and discuss my favorite moment from this entire episode,
在我们回到取证现场并讨论我这一集中最喜欢的时刻之前，

933
00:40:09.330 --> 00:40:10.730
I think we should take a break.
我觉得我们应该休息一下。

934
00:40:11.150 --> 00:40:12.630
What is your favorite moment?
你最喜欢的时刻是什么？

935
00:40:12.690 --> 00:40:13.630
I don't know.
我不知道。

936
00:40:14.010 --> 00:40:14.530
Okay, wait.
好吧，等等。

937
00:40:14.530 --> 00:40:15.510
I'll wait till after the break.
我等休息后再说。

938
00:40:15.630 --> 00:40:16.070
Okay, okay.
好吧，好吧。

939
00:40:16.490 --> 00:40:21.530
Let me just say the star of this episode is stenographer.
我只想说这一集的明星是速记员。

940
00:40:22.090 --> 00:40:22.770
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

941
00:40:23.070 --> 00:40:24.110
Okay, I know the one.
好吧，我知道是哪一段了。

942
00:40:24.250 --> 00:40:25.050
All right, we'll be back.
好了，我们马上回来。

943
00:40:25.050 --> 00:40:36.520
We are back.
我们回来了。

944
00:40:36.680 --> 00:40:42.780
And, Angela, during the break, I asked Sam to please pull this clip of the stenographer
安吉拉，在休息期间，我请萨姆调出了这段速记员的片段，

945
00:40:42.780 --> 00:40:46.480
reading back some of Michael's testimony.
她正在回读迈克尔的一些证词。

946
00:40:47.140 --> 00:40:47.440
Oh.
哦。

947
00:40:47.820 --> 00:40:52.380
So this happened right after a commercial break of the show.
这一幕发生在节目的广告插播之后。

948
00:40:52.600 --> 00:40:56.520
The first scene back was just the stenographer reading.
回来后的第一个镜头就是速记员在朗读。

949
00:40:56.800 --> 00:40:58.400
And it's so brilliant.
这真是太精彩了。

950
00:40:58.900 --> 00:40:59.820
Sam, will you play it?
萨姆，能播放一下吗？

951
00:41:00.760 --> 00:41:03.400
Mr. Scott, do you realize you just contradicted yourself?
斯科特先生，你意识到你刚才自相矛盾了吗？

952
00:41:03.400 --> 00:41:03.980
I did.
我意识到了。

953
00:41:04.120 --> 00:41:04.680
Yes, you did.
没错，你意识到了。

954
00:41:04.840 --> 00:41:05.800
Can I go to the bathroom?
我能去趟洗手间吗？

955
00:41:05.960 --> 00:41:06.140
No.
不行。

956
00:41:06.280 --> 00:41:07.000
I really have to.
我真的得去。

957
00:41:07.120 --> 00:41:08.360
I've been drinking lots of water.
我喝了很多水。

958
00:41:08.500 --> 00:41:09.800
You went five minutes ago.
你五分钟前才去过。

959
00:41:09.940 --> 00:41:11.160
That wasn't to go to the bathroom.
那次不是去洗手间。

960
00:41:11.200 --> 00:41:12.420
That was to get out of a question.
那是为了避开一个问题。

961
00:41:12.600 --> 00:41:13.880
You still have to answer it.
你还是得回答那个问题。

962
00:41:14.000 --> 00:41:15.060
First, can I go to the bathroom?
首先，我能去趟洗手间吗？

963
00:41:15.260 --> 00:41:15.440
No.
不行。

964
00:41:17.280 --> 00:41:18.400
She is perfection.
她简直完美。

965
00:41:18.820 --> 00:41:20.460
Lady, we got so much mail about her.
女士，我们收到了好多关于她的来信。

966
00:41:20.460 --> 00:41:25.300
Caitlin F., Brittany T., Lindsay H., Sarah C., who is the stenographer.
凯特琳·F、布兰妮·T、琳赛·H、莎拉·C，也就是那位速记员。

967
00:41:25.320 --> 00:41:26.660
She is fantastic.
她太棒了。

968
00:41:26.980 --> 00:41:31.140
How in the world did she repeat those lines back to the room with a straight face?
她到底是怎么做到面不改色地把那些台词复述给全场听的？

969
00:41:31.700 --> 00:41:34.480
And her cadence is so perfect.
而且她的语调把握得太完美了。

970
00:41:34.960 --> 00:41:37.080
Guys, her name is Valerie Ross.
伙计们，她叫瓦莱丽·罗斯。

971
00:41:37.300 --> 00:41:41.080
She most recently played the role of Eunice Simpson, O.J.
