01:03:26.260 --> 01:03:27.440
The butler gets it.
管家会去拿。

1431
01:03:27.880 --> 01:03:30.980
Tom Brady doesn't walk back to his bedroom for his cell phone.
汤姆·布雷迪才不会为了手机走回卧室呢。

1432
01:03:30.980 --> 01:03:32.740
He's too busy drinking water.
他忙着喝水呢。

1433
01:03:33.060 --> 01:03:33.960
He's too busy peeing.
他忙着上厕所呢。

1434
01:03:34.380 --> 01:03:42.180
Speaking of outstanding feats of athleticism, back in the conference room, Dwight is beating Jim at ping pong.
说到出色的运动表现，回到会议室，德怀特正在乒乓球比赛中打败吉姆。

1435
01:03:42.820 --> 01:03:46.740
Dwight looks like he's barely making any effort to beat Jim.
德怀特看起来几乎没怎么费力就赢了吉姆。

1436
01:03:46.900 --> 01:03:48.200
He's on his phone.
他还在玩手机。

1437
01:03:48.200 --> 01:03:50.140
He can just hit the ball no matter what.
无论如何他都能把球打回去。

1438
01:03:50.320 --> 01:03:53.680
And Pam comes in at 16 minutes, 21 seconds.
帕姆在16分21秒时进来了。

1439
01:03:54.220 --> 01:03:55.820
Jenna, I'm going to show you your outfit.
珍娜，我要给你看你的那身装扮。

1440
01:03:56.100 --> 01:03:57.460
I took a screen grab of it.
我截了图。

1441
01:03:57.600 --> 01:03:58.540
Oh, is it time?
噢，是时候了吗？

1442
01:03:58.540 --> 01:04:03.360
It's time because this is the moment if you really want to see your outfit here.
是时候了，因为如果你真的想看看你当时的装扮，现在就是时候了。

1443
01:04:03.680 --> 01:04:04.900
What is this outfit?
这身装扮怎么了？

1444
01:04:05.200 --> 01:04:07.040
What is your gripe about this outfit?
你对这身装扮有什么不满吗？

1445
01:04:07.220 --> 01:04:15.140
We have black tights, a long black skirt just below your knee, a blue buttoned up sweater.
我们有黑色连裤袜，一条刚好过膝的黑色长裙，还有一件蓝色扣子开衫。

1446
01:04:15.600 --> 01:04:21.820
I'm just saying, Pam went through this phase in the beginning of her courtship with Jim where she was zhuzhing herself up a little.
我只是说，帕姆在和吉姆刚开始交往时经历过一个阶段，那时候她会稍微打扮一下自己。

1447
01:04:22.020 --> 01:04:26.060
And I think this outfit says, I am now comfortable in my relationship.
我觉得这身装扮说明，我现在对这段关系感到自在了。

1448
01:04:26.380 --> 01:04:27.700
Do with that what you will.
你想怎么理解都行。

1449
01:04:27.700 --> 01:04:30.080
Well, I take it as an insult.
好吧，我把它当成一种冒犯。

1450
01:04:30.960 --> 01:04:32.820
It seems phrased that way.
听起来确实是那个意思。

1451
01:04:34.560 --> 01:04:37.720
I think maybe Pam is just a little cold.
我觉得帕姆可能只是有点冷。

1452
01:04:37.960 --> 01:04:38.760
It's winter.
现在是冬天。

1453
01:04:39.120 --> 01:04:45.280
She has exchanged her pantyhose for tights, which is something we did for her in the winter months.
她把连裤袜换成了紧身裤，这是我们冬天会为她做的事。

1454
01:04:45.280 --> 01:04:49.100
But I don't think she has gotten comfortable in any way.
但我觉得她并没有感到任何不自在。

1455
01:04:49.360 --> 01:04:53.660
She just had a day where maybe she didn't pair the right things together.
她只是那天可能没把衣服搭配好。

1456
01:04:53.660 --> 01:04:54.360
That is all.
仅此而已。

1457
01:04:54.580 --> 01:04:55.760
I think you'll see.
我想你会看到的。

1458
01:04:56.420 --> 01:05:00.860
In dinner party coming up, she's going to wear an adorable little cocktail dress.
在接下来的晚宴上，她会穿上一件可爱的小礼服。

1459
01:05:00.860 --> 01:05:01.640
So don't worry.
所以别担心。

1460
01:05:02.120 --> 01:05:02.440
All right.
好吧。

1461
01:05:02.560 --> 01:05:04.180
I will back off Pam's attire.
我不会再管帕姆的穿着了。

1462
01:05:04.380 --> 01:05:05.700
It did crack me up.
这确实把我逗乐了。

1463
01:05:05.980 --> 01:05:08.280
I have an observation about this scene.
我对这一幕有个观察。

1464
01:05:08.280 --> 01:05:11.240
Jim keeps saying spin serve.
吉姆一直在说旋转发球。

1465
01:05:11.540 --> 01:05:12.560
Spin serve.
旋转发球。

1466
01:05:12.980 --> 01:05:14.340
That is not a thing.
根本没这种说法。

1467
01:05:14.720 --> 01:05:15.660
I looked it up.
我查过了。

1468
01:05:16.380 --> 01:05:19.760
Spin is not reserved for a serve.
旋转并不是发球的专属。

1469
01:05:19.760 --> 01:05:26.920
And of the top five table tennis serves, only three of the five involve any spin.
在乒乓球的前五大发球中，只有三种涉及旋转。

1470
01:05:27.140 --> 01:05:28.420
And I'll tell you what they are.
我告诉你它们是什么。

1471
01:05:28.540 --> 01:05:31.700
Number one, the short side spin pendulum serve.
第一，短侧旋摆速发球。

1472
01:05:32.140 --> 01:05:36.260
Number two, the short side spin reverse pendulum serve.
第二，短侧旋反向摆速发球。

1473
01:05:36.260 --> 01:05:37.220
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1474
01:05:37.820 --> 01:05:41.360
Number three is the fast no spin cross serve.
第三是快速不转斜线发球。

1475
01:05:41.700 --> 01:05:45.860
Number four is the fast no spin down the line serve.
第四是快速不转直线发球。

1476
01:05:46.500 --> 01:05:49.720
And number five is the long side spin serve.
第五是长侧旋发球。

1477
01:05:49.980 --> 01:05:53.460
So there's no such thing as just spin serve.
所以根本没有所谓的旋转发球。

1478
01:05:53.720 --> 01:05:56.500
You have to be more specific, Jim.
你得说得更具体点，吉姆。

1479
01:05:56.920 --> 01:05:58.440
Is it a short side spin?
是短侧旋吗？

1480
01:05:58.640 --> 01:05:59.460
Is it a pendulum?
是摆速发球吗？

1481
01:05:59.860 --> 01:06:01.520
Is it a long side spin?
是长侧旋吗？

1482
01:06:02.060 --> 01:06:06.760
And by the way, just because you're putting spin on it doesn't mean you're mastering the game
顺便说一句，仅仅因为你加了旋转并不意味着你精通这项运动，

1483
01:06:06.760 --> 01:06:10.160
because there's a couple of great serves that involve no spin at all.
因为还有几种很棒的发球根本不带旋转。

1484
01:06:10.380 --> 01:06:15.780
I don't know why I felt the need to put Jim in his place about this spin serve,
我不知道为什么我非得就这个旋转发球的问题去纠正吉姆，

1485
01:06:15.920 --> 01:06:18.960
but he was just saying it with such authority.
但他说话的语气太笃定了。

1486
01:06:20.140 --> 01:06:21.680
And it's not a thing, Jim.
而且根本没这回事，吉姆。

1487
01:06:21.800 --> 01:06:22.260
It's not a thing.
没这回事。

1488
01:06:22.920 --> 01:06:26.400
Well, don't tell my husband that because he thinks the spin serve is where it's at.
好吧，别告诉我丈夫，因为他觉得旋转发球才是精髓。

1489
01:06:26.660 --> 01:06:28.860
He's going to spin it on over.
他打算把它旋转过去。

1490
01:06:29.960 --> 01:06:33.720
Listen, it's just that there needs to be more specificity.
听着，只是需要更具体一点。

1491
01:06:33.960 --> 01:06:38.580
Well, I'm going to tell him that next time he's playing while I'm trying to eat at the ping-pong table.
好吧，下次当我在乒乓球桌旁吃饭而他在打球时，我会告诉他的。

1492
01:06:38.740 --> 01:06:39.240
Please do.
请务必转达。

1493
01:06:39.320 --> 01:06:40.580
You put him in his place.
你去挫挫他的锐气。

1494
01:06:40.860 --> 01:06:42.640
Josh, that's not the long spin.
乔什，那不是长旋。

1495
01:06:43.320 --> 01:06:44.140
Side spin.
侧旋。

1496
01:06:44.540 --> 01:06:45.340
Short spin.
短旋。

1497
01:06:45.520 --> 01:06:46.520
That's a short spin.
那是短旋。

1498
01:06:46.860 --> 01:06:47.660
There you go.
这就对了。

1499
01:06:48.160 --> 01:06:49.620
Well, Jim says he's ready.
好吧，吉姆说他准备好了。

1500
01:06:50.000 --> 01:06:51.580
I'm going to go play Daryl.
我要去和达里尔打球了。

1501
01:06:51.700 --> 01:06:53.620
Pam's so excited they go down to the warehouse.
帕姆很兴奋，他们一起去了仓库。

1502
01:06:53.620 --> 01:07:00.460
And right away, it's not going Jim's way, and Kelly starts doing all of her smack talk, trash talk.
结果一开始就不顺吉姆的意，凯莉开始在那儿说些垃圾话，挑衅的话。

1503
01:07:00.640 --> 01:07:01.720
She's making up a song.
她还编了首歌。

1504
01:07:01.800 --> 01:07:04.220
Hey, hey, you, you, I don't like your boyfriend.
嘿，嘿，你，你，我不喜欢你男朋友。

1505
01:07:04.560 --> 01:07:05.760
She's doing a whole thing.
她在那儿搞得有模有样的。

1506
01:07:06.320 --> 01:07:07.140
Pam has had it.
帕姆忍无可忍了。

1507
01:07:07.460 --> 01:07:07.780
Yeah.
没错。

1508
01:07:08.120 --> 01:07:12.300
She's like, you and me, right now, we're going to play.
她就像是说，你和我，现在就来比一场。

1509
01:07:12.840 --> 01:07:14.280
And they are both horrible.
结果两人都打得烂透了。

1510
01:07:14.800 --> 01:07:16.080
We had a fan question.
我们有个粉丝提问。

1511
01:07:23.520 --> 01:07:25.080
Let me say this.
让我来说一下。

1512
01:07:25.420 --> 01:07:29.720
Mindy and I were not great at ping-pong, but we weren't that bad at ping-pong.
我和敏迪乒乓球打得并不好，但也没那么差。

1513
01:07:29.820 --> 01:07:33.340
So we were pretending to be that bad.
所以我们是假装打得那么差。

1514
01:07:33.440 --> 01:07:37.800
And the point was that we would never get past a certain number of volleys.
重点是我们得保证来回球数不超过某个数字。

1515
01:07:37.940 --> 01:07:39.620
Are they called volleys in ping-pong?
乒乓球里管那个叫来回球吗？

1516
01:07:39.960 --> 01:07:41.140
You should know.
你应该知道的。

1517
01:07:42.040 --> 01:07:42.980
Ho, ho.
呵，呵。

1518
01:07:43.240 --> 01:07:45.460
I didn't get that far in my research.
我的研究还没做到那一步。

1519
01:07:47.220 --> 01:07:53.200
And also, I know that John was actually good at ping-pong, and he had to pretend to be not as good as he was.
而且我知道约翰其实很擅长打乒乓球，他得假装自己没那么厉害。

1520
01:07:53.600 --> 01:07:53.860
Yes.
没错。

1521
01:07:54.140 --> 01:08:00.900
And by the way, we played a lot of ping-pong while we were just waiting for various camera setups and things like that.
顺便说一下，我们在等摄像机位调整之类的空档时，经常打乒乓球。

1522
01:08:01.040 --> 01:08:08.380
This was a really fun day of shooting, actually, because we had this toy, which then stayed in the warehouse and we would play.
其实那天拍摄特别开心，因为我们有了这个玩具，它后来就留在了仓库里，我们经常去玩。

1523
01:08:08.760 --> 01:08:14.320
Well, and there are a lot of deleted scenes of all the other office members playing ping-pong that didn't make it in.
嗯，还有很多其他办公室成员打乒乓球的删减片段没放进去。

1524
01:08:14.320 --> 01:08:18.700
And Phyllis and Stanley play at the makeshift ping-pong table up in the conference room.
菲利斯和斯坦利在会议室的临时乒乓球桌上打球。

1525
01:08:18.860 --> 01:08:20.200
Meredith has a turn.
梅雷迪斯也轮到了一次。

1526
01:08:20.480 --> 01:08:22.880
I yell off camera, I'm next!
我在镜头外大喊，下一个是我！

1527
01:08:22.880 --> 01:08:26.440
So it's like everyone is getting in there to play ping-pong.
所以感觉每个人都跑去打乒乓球了。

1528
01:08:27.160 --> 01:08:29.800
Lady, the deposition is almost over.
女士，取证环节快结束了。

1529
01:08:29.800 --> 01:08:41.900
And it's so sad, because they've read David Wallace's testimony about whether or not he was ever really going to hire Michael for this corporate position.
这太令人难过了，因为他们读了戴维·华莱士的证词，内容是关于他是否真的打算聘请迈克尔担任那个公司职位。

1530
01:08:42.100 --> 01:08:50.460
And you can tell in the testimony that David is really struggling to admit this, but the truth is, Michael was never a real contender.
从证词里你能听出来，戴维在承认这一点时非常挣扎，但事实是，迈克尔从来都不是真正的候选人。

1531
01:08:50.460 --> 01:08:54.140
Yeah, David says, listen, come on, he's a nice guy.
是啊，戴维说，听着，拜托，他是个好人。

1532
01:08:54.520 --> 01:08:55.060
Yeah.
没错。

1533
01:08:55.540 --> 01:09:01.400
And he didn't want to have to go on record saying, truthfully, Michael isn't anyone he considered.
他不想在记录里如实说出迈克尔根本不在他的考虑范围内。

1534
01:09:01.820 --> 01:09:10.580
But you know what's interesting is, of all of that crushing information, what Michael heard was that David Wallace called him a nice guy.
但你知道有趣的是什么吗？在所有那些令人心碎的信息中，迈克尔听到的只有戴维·华莱士说他是个好人。

1535
01:09:10.580 --> 01:09:24.400
Yeah, and when Jan's lawyer says, wouldn't you agree with Ms. Levinson that the company exhibits a pattern of disrespect towards its employees, Michael says, absolutely not.
没错，当简的律师问，你难道不同意莱文森女士所说的公司对员工表现出不尊重的模式吗，迈克尔说，绝对不同意。

1536
01:09:24.940 --> 01:09:27.660
Yeah, he tanks her lawsuit.
是啊，他搞砸了她的官司。

1537
01:09:28.060 --> 01:09:29.680
There goes the $4 million.
那四百万美元就这样没了。

1538
01:09:30.560 --> 01:09:33.940
Now they're only going to be able to get Chinese food for dinner.
现在他们晚饭只能吃得起中餐了。

1539
01:09:33.940 --> 01:09:36.640
Oh, it's going to be a rough car ride home.
哦，回家的车程肯定很难熬。

1540
01:09:36.840 --> 01:09:44.260
But there is a very sweet scene where David Wallace goes up to Michael and is like, hey, I'm really sorry that you got drug into this.
但有一个非常温馨的场景，戴维·华莱士走到迈克尔身边说，嘿，我很抱歉把你卷进这件事里。

1541
01:09:44.400 --> 01:09:45.440
I never wanted that.
我从来没想过这样。

1542
01:09:45.880 --> 01:09:47.220
And Michael's like, it's okay.
迈克尔说，没关系。

1543
01:09:47.640 --> 01:09:52.360
There is this moment, though, Jenna, where David is like the father Michael never had.
珍娜，那一刻，戴维就像是迈克尔从未拥有过的父亲。

1544
01:09:52.720 --> 01:09:55.140
And it looks like Michael is trying not to cry.
看起来迈克尔在努力忍住不哭。

1545
01:09:55.340 --> 01:09:55.500
Yeah.
没错。

1546
01:09:55.640 --> 01:09:58.440
Like when your dad comes up to you and says, I'm sorry, buddy.
就像你爸爸走过来对你说，我很抱歉，伙计。

1547
01:09:58.680 --> 01:09:59.080
You okay?
你还好吗？

1548
01:09:59.360 --> 01:10:00.220
It's like that moment.
就是那种时刻。

1549
01:10:00.680 --> 01:10:00.880
Yeah.
没错。

1550
01:10:00.880 --> 01:10:05.080
And Michael's like, for the record, I think you're a nice guy, too.
迈克尔说，郑重声明，我觉得你也是个好人。

1551
01:10:05.440 --> 01:10:07.340
It's a really sweet scene.
这真是一个非常温馨的场景。

1552
01:10:07.780 --> 01:10:08.380
It is.
确实。

1553
01:10:08.680 --> 01:10:14.040
I have a great little behind-the-scenes trivia for you for that car ride home with Michael and Jan.
关于迈克尔和简开车回家的那段戏，我有一个很棒的幕后小花絮要告诉你。

1554
01:10:14.380 --> 01:10:15.280
Ooh, tell me.
噢，快告诉我。

1555
01:10:15.680 --> 01:10:20.760
Lester said that they had put lipstick cameras in the PT Cruiser for that car ride home.
莱斯特说，为了拍摄那段回家路上的戏，他们在PT巡洋舰车里安装了口红摄像机。

1556
01:10:21.000 --> 01:10:21.400
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1557
01:10:21.780 --> 01:10:25.760
And when they got the footage back, it was all just completely dark.
结果等他们拿到素材一看，画面全是一片漆黑。

1558
01:10:25.760 --> 01:10:30.880
The little light that they had put in the car, like on the dashboard where you couldn't see it,
他们原本在车里仪表盘上装了一个小灯，位置很隐蔽，你看不到它，

1559
01:10:31.040 --> 01:10:33.920
it was going to illuminate Melora and Steve's faces.
本意是用来照亮梅洛拉和史蒂夫的脸。

1560
01:10:34.160 --> 01:10:39.640
I guess there was something wrong with the light, and it clicked off, and all the footage was dark.
我猜是灯出了什么故障，自动熄灭了，所以所有的素材都是黑的。

1561
01:10:39.800 --> 01:10:40.300
Oh, no.
噢，天哪。

1562
01:10:40.400 --> 01:10:48.040
So the only footage they had of that car ride scene was from the follow car that was in front of them, right?
所以他们当时唯一拍到的那段开车戏，其实是来自前面那辆跟拍车的镜头，对吧？

1563
01:10:48.360 --> 01:10:48.760
Yes.
没错。

1564
01:10:48.760 --> 01:10:54.380
So they had a car in front of them filming them, and that's the only camera that worked.
所以他们有一辆车在前面拍摄，那是唯一正常工作的摄像机。

1565
01:10:54.760 --> 01:10:57.120
And I actually really like it.
而且我其实真的很喜欢这种效果。

1566
01:10:57.220 --> 01:11:02.280
And they talked about this a little bit in the commentary that it made it seem just way more real.
他们在评论音轨里也稍微提过，这让画面看起来真实多了。

1567
01:11:02.580 --> 01:11:03.220
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1568
01:11:03.220 --> 01:11:08.840
That there was this distance between the camera and what was happening, kind of like what Randall
摄像机和拍摄对象之间保持了一定的距离，就像兰德尔

1569
01:11:08.840 --> 01:11:10.560
talked about when he was on.
上节目时提到的那样。

1570
01:11:10.780 --> 01:11:14.680
The further away you were, the more intimate the moment feels to the viewer.
你离得越远，观众反而会觉得那一刻越亲密。

1571
01:11:15.120 --> 01:11:15.580
Absolutely.
绝对是这样。

1572
